{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Register the tool under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":". The key is the tool name."}]},{"type":"code","value":"toolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.city}</p>,\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.input"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.output"},{"type":"text","value":" are typed from the tool's schemas. You do not cast them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-problem-with-one-line","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The problem with one line"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool call is not one event. It arrives in stages: the model names the tool, streams the arguments, then the result comes back. A component that only reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.output"},{"type":"text","value":" renders nothing for most of that time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.state"},{"type":"text","value":" instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"full-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: ({ part }) => {\n      if (part.state === 'input-streaming') return <p>Looking up weather</p>\n      if (part.state === 'input-complete') return <p>Checking {part.input?.city}</p>\n      if (part.state === 'error') return <p>Weather lookup failed</p>\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return (\n          <dl>\n            <dt>{part.input?.city}</dt>\n            <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n          </dl>\n        )\n      }\n      return null\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function WeatherChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=weather-tool"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool now shows progress while it runs, and a definition list when it finishes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-states-you-care-about","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The states you care about"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What to show"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"awaiting-input"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The call started. No arguments yet."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-streaming"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model is still writing the arguments. Show a spinner."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input-complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arguments are final. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.input"},{"type":"text","value":" is safe to read."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"complete"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The result arrived. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.output"},{"type":"text","value":" is safe to read."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The call failed. Show your own copy."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two more states apply only to tools that need approval: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-requested"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval-responded"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"./tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool approval"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"move-it-to-its-own-file","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Move it to its own file"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool map grows fast. Type the props with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolProps"},{"type":"text","value":" and the component lives anywhere."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function WeatherTool({\n  part,\n}: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>) {\n  if (part.state !== 'complete') return null\n  return <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=weather-tool"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second type argument is the tool name. Pass it, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.input"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.output"},{"type":"text","value":" narrow to that tool's schemas."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool that needs a yes or no first? See "},{"type":"link","href":"./tool-approval","children":[{"type":"text","value":"tool approval"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formatting text, thinking, or images? Register them under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partsComponents"},{"type":"text","value":". See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-problem-with-one-line","text":"The problem with one line","level":2},{"id":"full-example","text":"Full example","level":2},{"id":"the-states-you-care-about","text":"The states you care about","level":2},{"id":"move-it-to-its-own-file","text":"Move it to its own file","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nRegister the tool under `toolsComponents`. The key is the tool name.\n\n```tsx ignore\ntoolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.city}</p>,\n}\n```\n\n`part.input` and `part.output` are typed from the tool's schemas. You do not cast them.\n\n## The problem with one line\n\nA tool call is not one event. It arrives in stages: the model names the tool, streams the arguments, then the result comes back. A component that only reads `part.output` renders nothing for most of that time.\n\nBranch on `part.state` instead.\n\n## Full example\n\n```tsx group=weather-tool\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: ({ part }) => {\n      if (part.state === 'input-streaming') return <p>Looking up weather</p>\n      if (part.state === 'input-complete') return <p>Checking {part.input?.city}</p>\n      if (part.state === 'error') return <p>Weather lookup failed</p>\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return (\n          <dl>\n            <dt>{part.input?.city}</dt>\n            <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n          </dl>\n        )\n      }\n      return null\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function WeatherChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\nThe tool now shows progress while it runs, and a definition list when it finishes.\n\n## The states you care about\n\n| `part.state` | What to show |\n| --- | --- |\n| `awaiting-input` | The call started. No arguments yet. |\n| `input-streaming` | The model is still writing the arguments. Show a spinner. |\n| `input-complete` | Arguments are final. `part.input` is safe to read. |\n| `complete` | The result arrived. `part.output` is safe to read. |\n| `error` | The call failed. Show your own copy. |\n\nTwo more states apply only to tools that need approval: `approval-requested` and `approval-responded`. See [tool approval](./tool-approval).\n\n## Move it to its own file\n\nA tool map grows fast. Type the props with `ToolProps` and the component lives anywhere.\n\n```tsx group=weather-tool\nimport type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function WeatherTool({\n  part,\n}: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>) {\n  if (part.state !== 'complete') return null\n  return <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n}\n```\n\nThe second type argument is the tool name. Pass it, and `part.input` and `part.output` narrow to that tool's schemas.\n\n## Next\n\n- A tool that needs a yes or no first? See [tool approval](./tool-approval).\n- Formatting text, thinking, or images? Register them under `partsComponents`. See the [React guide](../react).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Make a tool look right\nid: ui-recipe-format-a-tool\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Register a component for one tool, and branch on the tool call state so it never shows raw JSON.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - toolsComponents\n  - ToolProps\n  - tool call state\n  - example\n---\n\nRegister the tool under `toolsComponents`. The key is the tool name.\n\n```tsx ignore\ntoolsComponents: {\n  getWeather: ({ part }) => <p>{part.input?.city}</p>,\n}\n```\n\n`part.input` and `part.output` are typed from the tool's schemas. You do not cast them.\n\n## The problem with one line\n\nA tool call is not one event. It arrives in stages: the model names the tool, streams the arguments, then the result comes back. A component that only reads `part.output` renders nothing for most of that time.\n\nBranch on `part.state` instead.\n\n## Full example\n\n```tsx group=weather-tool\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { createChatHook } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'getWeather',\n  description: 'Look up weather',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ city: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ temperature: z.number() }),\n}).client()\n\nconst chatOptions = {\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  tools: [getWeather],\n}\n\nconst { useAppChat } = createChatHook({\n  options: chatOptions,\n  components: {\n    layout: ({ Messages }) => <main><Messages /></main>,\n    message: ({ Parts }) => <article><Parts /></article>,\n  },\n  partsComponents: {\n    text: ({ part }) => <p>{part.content}</p>,\n    fallback: () => null,\n  },\n  toolsComponents: {\n    getWeather: ({ part }) => {\n      if (part.state === 'input-streaming') return <p>Looking up weather</p>\n      if (part.state === 'input-complete') return <p>Checking {part.input?.city}</p>\n      if (part.state === 'error') return <p>Weather lookup failed</p>\n      if (part.state === 'complete') {\n        return (\n          <dl>\n            <dt>{part.input?.city}</dt>\n            <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n          </dl>\n        )\n      }\n      return null\n    },\n  },\n})\n\nexport function WeatherChat() {\n  const chat = useAppChat()\n  return <chat.AppChat />\n}\n```\n\nThe tool now shows progress while it runs, and a definition list when it finishes.\n\n## The states you care about\n\n| `part.state` | What to show |\n| --- | --- |\n| `awaiting-input` | The call started. No arguments yet. |\n| `input-streaming` | The model is still writing the arguments. Show a spinner. |\n| `input-complete` | Arguments are final. `part.input` is safe to read. |\n| `complete` | The result arrived. `part.output` is safe to read. |\n| `error` | The call failed. Show your own copy. |\n\nTwo more states apply only to tools that need approval: `approval-requested` and `approval-responded`. See [tool approval](./tool-approval).\n\n## Move it to its own file\n\nA tool map grows fast. Type the props with `ToolProps` and the component lives anywhere.\n\n```tsx group=weather-tool\nimport type { ToolProps } from '@tanstack/ai-react/ui'\n\nexport function WeatherTool({\n  part,\n}: ToolProps<typeof chatOptions, 'getWeather'>) {\n  if (part.state !== 'complete') return null\n  return <dd>{part.output?.temperature}&deg;</dd>\n}\n```\n\nThe second type argument is the tool name. Pass it, and `part.input` and `part.output` narrow to that tool's schemas.\n\n## Next\n\n- A tool that needs a yes or no first? See [tool approval](./tool-approval).\n- Formatting text, thinking, or images? Register them under `partsComponents`. See the [React guide](../react).\n"}
